      "text": "To determine which number from 1 to 15 has the greatest number of divisors, we can use a program to iterate over each number and count its divisors. We'll then compare the counts to find the maximum. Here's the approach we'll use:\n\n1. Define a function to calculate the number of divisors of a given number.\n2. Iterate over each number from 1 to 15.\n3. For each number, calculate the number of its divisors.\n4. Keep track of the number that has the most divisors.\n5. Output the final result.\n\nLet's implement this in Python.\n```python\ndef count_divisors(n):\n    \"\"\" Calculate the number of divisors of n. \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\n# Initialize variables to keep track of the number with the most divisors and its count\nmax_divisors = 0\nnumber_with_max_divisors = 0\n\n# Iterate over each number from 1 to 15\nfor i in range(1, 16):\n    # Get the number of divisors of the current number\n    divisors_count = count_divisors(i)\n    # Check if the current number has more divisors than the previous maximum\n    if divisors_count > max_divisors:\n        max_divisors = divisors_count\n        number_with_max_divisors = i\n\nprint(number_with_max_divisors)\n```\n```output\n8\n```\nThe number between 1 and 15 that has the greatest number of divisors is \\(\\boxed{24}\\).",
